# M38: never translate line endings. The Windows runners compile .mc sources
# and run shell scripts straight out of the checkout, and GitHub Windows images
# ship core.autocrlf=true -- a `#!/bin/sh\r` is a hard failure. The lexer treats
# \r as whitespace, so a CRLF checkout would still produce the same tokens and
# the same object, but the scripts are not so forgiving (docs/specs/M38.md § 7).
* -text
